<%# Only rendered above the composer while the conversation has no
    messages yet (see show.html.erb) — a returning guest with history
    already has better ways to say what they need than a chip list built
    for a blank slate. Tapping a chip only ever fills the composer's
    textarea (chat_composer_controller.js#fillFromChip); it never submits
    anything by itself, so a request the guest didn't read and confirm can
    never be sent. Free typing is always available regardless. %>
<%# A single horizontal row that scrolls sideways, rather than a wrapping
    block. Wrapped chips on a narrow phone grew to three or four rows and
    pushed the composer off the bottom of the screen; one row costs a fixed
    amount of vertical space no matter how many categories a hotel has
    configured, which is the number this page cannot predict.

    min-h-11 (44px) on each chip: the old ones measured 34px, below the size
    a thumb hits reliably, and these are the first thing a guest touches. %>
<div id="quick-actions" class="shrink-0" role="group"
     aria-label="<%= t("guest.chats.quick_actions.heading") %>">
  <div class="flex gap-2 overflow-x-auto overscroll-x-contain px-4 pb-2 [scrollbar-width:none] [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden">
    <% quick_actions.each_with_index do |action, index| %>
      <button type="button" id="quick-action-<%= index %>" dir="auto"
              class="min-h-11 shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap rounded-full border px-4 text-sm font-medium
                     active:opacity-70"
              style="border-color:var(--brand-secondary)"
              data-action="click->chat-composer#fillFromChip"
              data-prefill-text="<%= action.prefill %>">
        <%= action.label %>
      </button>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
